# Copy this file to `.env.local` and replace the values with your own
# from Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys.
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored, so your real keys stay on your machine.
# Never commit a real key.
#
# Which key do I want?
#   - "Publishable key", starts with sb_publishable_   <- this one
#   - Older projects call it the "anon" key and it starts with eyJ...
#     Both are low-privilege and safe to expose in the browser. Supabase renamed
#     it, and projects created after Nov 2025 only have the new one.
#   - Do NOT use a "Secret key" (sb_secret_...). It bypasses Row Level Security
#     and would hand anyone who loads the page full access to the database.
#
# What the key does and does not protect you:
#   It is safe to publish, but it is NOT a login. It only grants what your Row
#   Level Security policies in supabase/schema.sql allow - and right now those
#   policies allow everything, so treat the key as public.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_replace-with-your-key
